e** as nine independent dry runs.\n    87\t  In the applied sequence the extractor **re-dry-runs each cluster against the tree after the\n    88\t  previous cluster's commit**, takes a fresh snapshot `.refactor/engine-cNN-before.json`\n    89\t  (`python3 $S/snapshot_bodies.py snapshot scripts/forge/forge_cli --out .refactor/engine-cNN-before.json` — scope exactly `scripts/forge/forge_cli`, the gate's `--pkg`; including `tests` makes the oracle fail on unmanifested files: critic blocking finding 1),\n    90\t  then applies. Bindings and destination imports are identical between baseline and sequential\n    91\t  dry runs; only `remove_imports` grows (an import is removed when its *last* reader leaves\n    92\t  `_engine.py`, which for shared names happens in a later cluster). Both values are listed.\n    93\t- Gate environment (critic blocking finding 2; without `PYTHONPATH`/`MYPYPATH` the `types` step reports 3 new `import-untyped` errors and the gate FAILs): run from the repo root as\n    94\t  `env -u FORGE_SESSION_PID -u REFACTOR_TYPE_CMD PYTHONPATH=scripts:scripts/forge MYPYPATH=scripts:scripts/forge TMPDIR=/dev/shm/forge-gate PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\" bash $S/verify.sh ...`\n    95\t  (same variables the app split's `.refactor/split-app.workflow.js` GATE_ENV exported; `REFACTOR_TEST_CMD` and `REFACTOR_MINT_CMD` come from the launching shell). Verified on the untouched tree: `types ok: 251 error(s), all grandfathered`.\n    96\t- Verify (after apply, before commit), with `REFACTOR_TEST_CMD` already exported\n    97\t  (`tests.test_cli_chain tests.test_cli_chain_finalize tests.test_revision9_cli_surfaces tests.test_cli_loader`):\n    98\t  `bash $S/verify.sh --pkg scripts/forge/forge_cli --snapshot .refactor/engine-cNN-before.json --manifest .refactor/engine-<x>.json --strict-bodies`\n    99\t  `verify.sh` runs ruff, `check_file_length.py` (honours `.refactor-baseline.json` in cwd, so the\n   100\t  shrinking grandfathered `_engine.py` passes at every step), the mypy ratchet\n   101\t  (`type_baseline.py check`, baseline keyed by *(code, message)* so the five grandfathered\n   102\t  `_engine.py` entries keep matching after they move files), `lint-imports`, and the focused tests.\n   103\t- Expected refusals: **none** for any cluster (all nine dry runs verified; the refusal classes in\n   104\t  `operations.md` — property setters, stacked/undeclared decorators, name mangling, `super`,\n   105\t  `__class__`, globals still defined in the source, destination import-name clash — do not\n   106\t  occur: inventory `reasons: []` for all 41 methods, `mangled: []`, and no method name collides\n   107\t  with a destination import).\n   108\t- Commit message form: `refactor(engine): move <cluster> verbs to _verbs_<x>.py (tier 1, function shape)`.\n   109\t  Every cluster commit touches `*.py` → the project changelog gate needs one `## [Unreleased]`\n   110\t  line staged with it.\n   111\t\n   112\t### Prerequisite config commit P0 (before c01, config only, no code moved)\n   113\t\n   114\t`verify.sh` runs `ruff check scripts/forge/forge_cli`; a new `_verbs_*.py` gets the full rule\n   115\tset, so the grandfathered findings that today hide under the `_engine.py` per-file-ignores entry\n   390\t   modules are enumerated automatically, and each imports its controls by value like `_engine.py`\n   391\t   does today. Check `tests.test_cli_loader` (in the focused set) passes at every cluster.\n   392\t5. **Type ratchet keyed by (code, message), not file.** Five grandfathered `_engine.py` entries\n   393\t   (`_engine.py:1638,1643,1867,2536,3700`) move to `_verbs_gate`/`_verbs_gate_evals`/\n   394\t   `_verbs_review_collect`/`_verbs_finalize` with the same messages. Simulation: no new keys. If\n   395\t   the gate shows `import-untyped codex_orchestrator` ×3, the gate environment above was not applied — a FAIL step is a failed gate; rerun with the environment, not a\n   396\t   move (identical on the untouched tree); do not \"fix